A||N||3||Seanh||Stripped Caliper slid bolt, what to do???||||11||
Z||000000||Seanh||06-18-2001||09:20 PM||||Sh!t! I just stripped a front caliper mounting/slide pin torx head. Anyone got any bright ideas on how to get the damn thing out? Thanks!||||reg||11
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||06-18-2001||09:33 PM||||Hey Sean!<BR>It is easy!<BR>Start by removing the outer pad, and put your c-clamp on the caliper like you normally do, but protect the rotor if you want to save it...<BR>Press the piston back in and the head of the slide bolt will be visible now...<BR>Take your vise grips and wrench it out!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||06-18-2001||10:35 PM||||yes vice grips will do the trick.sean make sure they are metric vice grips hehe.Hey also take your time with this little project of yours try to enjoy this work you are doing to your car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||06-19-2001||01:45 AM||||Yep, vice grips worked. I got it out finally. Hehehe...Now I broke 3 of the 4 bolts that hold the sway bar on. There pretty much rusted in there. Its now obvious that none of these front end component have ever been removed until now. Any bright ideas on how to get that sway bar bolts out? I was going to use an e-z-out, but not sure which size, any reccomendations? Thanks||||reg||1
